From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Launcher3: an application just installed is on the screen in front of you

An application installed on this device went onto a page that did not exist
until it was made for it, which on this device is a page nobody can find.

AddWorkspaceItemsTask looks for a cell from screen index 1 upward, and never
offers screen 0 one. On a phone that is right: there are several screens, and
screen 0 is the one the search box and the widgets are on. Here there is one
screen (0012), so the search found nothing, made a second page at the end and
put the application there -- and the way to that page is a sideways swipe that
nothing on the screen suggests. The caret above the hotseat is out (0006), the
line AOSP draws under the pages sits at alpha 0 until a scroll moves it, so it
answers a swipe rather than inviting one, and an indicator is not wanted ("那个
指示器我让去掉了", user, 2026-10-22). The requirement is the plain one: an
application you install is on the home screen ("只要安装后应用程序出现在首页也
保留", user, 2026-10-22).

So the search starts at screen 0. The layout leaves seven of its twelve cells
free (0014), and what fills them is what the reader installs.

Row 0 of that screen is the search box and not an item of the model, so the
search marks it occupied, the way LoaderCursor does when it reads the
workspace. Without that, the first application installed would be written into
the cell behind the box and dropped by the next load rather than shown -- a
question AOSP never had to answer here, having never placed anything on this
screen.

Nothing else changes. If screen 0 is full the search goes on to the screens
after it exactly as before, and still makes one at the end when they are all
full.

This is the second half of what the user asked for. The first is that the
application takes the place of the entry that installed it, wherever that entry
is (WeReadInstaller/HomeScreenCell.java); this is where everything else goes,
and neither of them is about any particular application.

